# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""CMS I Exam 5 EXAM-STYLE II pool B -- Lectures 26-28 (Venous Disorders, Arterial Occlusive
Disease & Aneurysms, Cardiomyopathy). 70 new items for the 2 x 70 exam-style forms.

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.

WHY (Jaxon, 2026-10-29, after the real Exam 5): the paper had (1) vignettes of patients with
SEVERAL comorbidities where similar drugs or diseases were told apart by contraindication, and the
student had to pick what to use instead; and (2) guideline-score questions: a vignette, then
"what is the score?". This pool is written in exactly those two shapes:
  kind "score"      the student computes or classifies from the vignette (Wells criteria for deep
                    vein thrombosis from the s55 pictures, ankle-brachial index arithmetic from s43,
                    Rutherford class from the s65 table);
  kind "guideline"  a size / percentage / level in the vignette decides the action (aneurysm
                    surveillance and repair, carotid stenosis, blood pressure and lipid targets,
                    ejection fraction, B-type natriuretic peptide, wall thickness, sodium limit);
  kind "comorbid"   several conditions at once; a contraindication, a look-alike disease or a
                    shared cause decides which option fits THIS patient.
Explanations follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md (the 2026-10-29 standard).

Slides only. The scope rules of the shipped pools are respected (cms_e5l26/27/28_scope.py):
  - Wells: never a total of exactly zero in a stem or option; "previously documented DVT" is in
    the s55 calculator picture but NOT in the s55 table picture, so no stem has a prior clot;
    travel is a risk factor (s49) but not a Wells item; pulmonary embolism Wells is not in the
    deck (respiratory block), so none.
  - Ankle-brachial index values sit well inside a band, never 0.4, 0.9 or 1.3.
  - Rutherford IIA is never keyed (its arterial Doppler is contested, s62 vs s65); every
    Rutherford item keys IIB or III, and IIA explanations never lean on the Doppler.
  - Aneurysm sizes never sit on a threshold (women 5.2, men 3.4 / 4.1->4.7, thoracic 5.0 / 5.8).
  - NYHA class is excluded (L28 s14 belongs to L25), so Lecture 28 has no class-scoring item.
  - Dilated cardiomyopathy ejection fractions are far from 40% (20-25%); digoxin is keyed only as
    a positive inotrope to AVOID in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.

Fields beyond the usual Q(): lec ("l26" | "l27" | "l28"), kind (above), slot, lead, and for
ordered non-numeric option sets `order` (the display order the partitioner must keep: Rutherford
classes I -> III, Wells likelihood low -> high). Numeric option sets are ordered by
tools/_option_order.py. The key is authored first (Q() requires it).
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from _cmse3_q import Q
import cms_e5l26_scope as S26
import cms_e5l27_scope as S27
import cms_e5l28_scope as S28

D26, D27, D28 = S26.DECK, S27.DECK, S28.DECK


def cite(*parts):
    """cite((D26, "54-55"), (D27, "47")) -> 'Deck, Slides 54-55; Deck, Slide 47'."""
    out = []
    for deck, sl in parts:
        sl = str(sl)
        out.append("%s, Slide%s %s" % (deck, "s" if ("," in sl or "-" in sl) else "", sl))
    return "; ".join(out)


def X(lec, kind, topic, io, q, opts, cite_, slot, lead, order=None):
    d = Q(topic, io, q, opts, cite_)
    d.update(lec=lec, kind=kind, slot=slot, lead=lead)
    if order:
        assert sorted(order) == sorted(o[0] for o in opts), "order must list every option: %s" % q[:60]
        d["order"] = order
    return d


